PURPOSE
H12 established that candidate structural directions should earn permanent capacity through repeated functional causal consequence.

H13 attacks a limitation of testing one direction at a time.

QUESTION
What if:

candidate A alone
does not improve function,

candidate B alone
does not improve function,

but

A + B together
create a useful developmental representation?

A purely individual structural-credit gate would reject both.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- prove real Yggdrasil requires bilinear structural interactions;
- freeze pairwise search;
- justify an all-pairs permanent interaction graph;
- solve combinatorial structure search;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

