PRIMARY NON-ADDITIVE POSITIVE
One-at-a-time causal structural credit says:

DO NOT GROW 0.

DO NOT GROW 1.

But pairwise causal credit says:

GROW 0 + 1 TOGETHER.

Therefore:

STRUCTURAL UTILITY IS NOT GUARANTEED TO BE ADDITIVE.

A permanent-memory controller that evaluates only individual dimensions can miss useful compositional structure.

