->

STRUCTURAL UTILITY CREDIT

then

PERSISTENCE-GATED PERMANENT WRITE.

H13 adds:

candidate structures may need to be:
COMPOSITE.

But composite candidate generation must remain bounded.

IMPORTANT LIMITATION
The cooperative target is explicitly bilinear.

Real useful structural interactions may be:
- additive;
- multiplicative;
- conditional;
- higher-order;
- spatial;
- temporal.

H13 proves only that individual utility testing is insufficient in principle.

It does not establish bilinear pairs as the preferred representation.

DECISION
AR-H13 is POSITIVE WITH A COMBINATORIAL-SEARCH LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- useful permanent structure can be non-additive;
- individual structural credit can reject every member of a useful pair;
- cooperative causal probes can recover the pair;
- one-shot cooperative tests create strong multiple-comparison risk;
- persistence controls false structural growth;
- exhaustive pair search violates bounded-resource scaling;
- fixed probe budgets produce rapidly increasing discovery latency.

Not demonstrated:

- real Yggdrasil cooperative structural dimensions;
- a scalable candidate-generation rule;
- higher-order interaction search;
- safe structural search in mature high-value regions;
- optimal persistence under large candidate sets.

NEXT CLEAN QUESTION
AR-H14 — BOUNDED COMPOSITE CANDIDATE GENERATION

Question:

Can local residual / eligibility statistics nominate a SMALL subset of candidate interactions
before expensive functional pair probing?

Desired:

do not test every pair.

Candidate nomination signals may include:
- persistent joint eligibility;
- residual co-activation;
- conditional consequence dependence;
- repeated failure of individual models;
- spatial/temporal adjacency.

Compare:

A.
exhaustive pair search;

B.
random bounded pair search;

C.
local nomination then causal confirmation;

D.
failure under misleading correlated residuals.

The nomination stage must not itself authorize permanent growth.

It only decides:

WHAT IS WORTH SPENDING CAUSAL STRUCTURAL PROBES ON?

Permanent write still requires H12-style functional causal consequence.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

